            <ArticleTitle>[Headache in childhood: clinico-epidemiologic study. Preliminary communication: The headache risk].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1251-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After a review of the attempt to relate headache risk factors to the Periodic Syndrome, preliminary data from a clinical epidemiological survey of 980 children (449 M and 531 F aged 4-14 with Idiopathic Headache are reported. The importance of HRFs as predictors of headache is emphasised as is the need to start prophylaxis before headache attacks begin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
